---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = '/for/print-on-demand';
const title = 'Shopify cart recovery for print-on-demand stores';
const desc = 'Recover the exact design and personalization without promising an unconfirmed production date.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/for">Explore related guides</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify cart recovery for print-on-demand stores</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Recover the exact design and personalization without promising an unconfirmed production date.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Preserve the production-ready choice</h2>
<p>A saved product name is insufficient for a custom order. Require the chosen garment, size, color, print placement and personalization to survive the return link. Where artwork or a preview needs approval, make that approval step clear. Do not expose private personalization in a subject line or lock-screen preview.</p>
<h2>Resolve uncertainty before offering a code</h2>
<p>Link to the actual size chart, print-care instructions and policy for personalized returns. Distinguish production lead time from carrier transit time; confirm both with the fulfillment partner before promising arrival. A design-drop reminder should reflect actual availability and rights to use the artwork, rather than manufactured scarcity.</p>
<h2>Choose controls for split fulfillment</h2>
<p>Ask a candidate to demonstrate a mixed basket containing a custom item and stocked merchandise. Show shipping charges and production status without implying both arrive together. Keep creator launch campaigns from competing with a queued cart offer. Sequenzy can remain a candidate for email workflow evaluation, but require a demonstration of the Shopify and fulfillment data needed here before selecting it.</p>
<h2>Model the cost of a remake</h2>
<p>Use actual blank, print, pick-pack, shipping subsidy and expected remake costs when setting an incentive ceiling. A percentage of gross margin is not the same as a percentage discount on revenue. Keep creator royalties and multi-parcel delivery in the calculation; a higher recovered order count can still lose contribution.</p>
<h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
<p>Create a personalized shirt plus a stocked accessory, change the size, and open the saved link after the production cutoff. Inspect artwork persistence, variant, total shipping and delivery wording. Then purchase from another session and inspect queued follow-ups. These are proposed checks, not completed tests.</p>
<h2>Related decisions</h2>
<p>Compare <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">fashion variant recovery</a> with <a class="link" href="/for/subscription-boxes">subscription box commitments</a>. A print approval is a different job from a recurring plan or a garment stock alert.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
